name: WebDAVHandler
description: Filesystem handler for WebDAV and Nextcloud servers
version: @VERSION@
date: @DATE@
author: orgin
submitter: orgin
email:
url:
category: driver/handler
replaces:
requirements: clib4.library 2.5, AmiSSL 5, filesysbox.library 54.8
license: Public domain
minosversion: 4.1
texttype: Plain text
distribute: yes
hend:

webdav-handler shows your WebDAV servers on one volume on AmigaOS 4,
WebDAV: (device WDV:). Every server you add with the prefs program
wdvprefs is a drawer in it, connected when the drawer is first opened.
Files can be opened, copied, renamed, deleted and saved directly on the
server, from Workbench, the Shell and any program. Nextcloud, ownCloud,
NAS boxes, hosting services and web servers such as Apache work; on
Nextcloud the handler also keeps file dates and uploads big files in
parts.

This is the new name of Nextcloud Handler (up to 0.39).

Features:

- Any number of servers in one device, set up with the prefs program
  wdvprefs ("Test connection" button included). Each server's type is
  found by itself (Nextcloud or plain WebDAV) or can be set.
- Encrypted connections (https) through AmiSSL, with certificate check;
  a server's own certificate can be given.
- Files of any size; on Nextcloud big files are uploaded in parts, so
  server limits on request size do not matter.
- National characters in file names, converted between the Amiga
  character set and UTF-8.
- Upper and lower case are ignored, as on any Amiga volume.
- Comments (FileNote) are kept on the server; on Nextcloud also file
  dates (Copy CLONE, SetDate).
- The password can be asked for with a requester and remembered.
- The volume can be mounted at boot: a server is connected on first use,
  and reconnected by itself after network problems.
- A failed upload is reported with a requester, and the data is kept
  locally, so nothing is lost.
- OS 4.1 style icons, with a volume icon for WDV:.

Requirements (install these first):

- AmigaOS 4.1 Final Edition (tested with Update 3).
- filesysbox.library 54.8 or newer (part of AmigaOS 4.1 FE).
- clib4.library 2.5 or newer:
  OS4Depot development/library/misc/clib4.lha
  or https://github.com/AmigaLabs/clib4/releases
- AmiSSL 5 or newer:
  OS4Depot library/misc/amissl.lha
  or https://github.com/jens-maus/amissl/releases
- A TCP/IP stack (Roadshow, as included in AmigaOS 4.1).

Installation:

Double-click the Install icon. It checks the requirements, copies the
handler to L: and wdvprefs to SYS:Prefs, installs the DOSDriver WDV and
the volume icon, mounts WDV: and starts wdvprefs to add your servers.
Everything else is described in WebDAVHandler.guide.

Upgrading from Nextcloud Handler: the Install script offers to remove it,
and wdvprefs takes its servers over (the server list of 0.38/0.39 and the
DOSDrivers of 0.37 and older) and offers to delete the old settings.

History:

- 0.41 (2026-11-17): Nextcloud Handler is now WebDAV Handler
  (webdav-handler, device WDV:, volume WebDAV:, prefs wdvprefs); any WebDAV
  server works and Nextcloud servers keep their extras. A Type for every
  server (Automatic, Nextcloud, WebDAV). Install removes Nextcloud Handler
  on request and wdvprefs takes its servers over. OS 4.1 style icons and a
  volume icon for WDV:. Setting a date on a server that cannot keep it is
  accepted without effect. Reading files with a weak ETag works. With
  clib4.library older than 2.5 the handler shows a requester instead of
  stopping the boot.
- 0.39 (2026-11-17, Nextcloud Handler): one device, NCH:, for all servers:
  every server is a drawer, connected when it is first used. The new prefs
  program nchprefs keeps the server list (with "Test connection") and takes
  over the servers of the old DOSDrivers. Remembered passwords go into the
  server list. The character set of file names comes from ENV:Charset when
  CHARSET is not given. Long server messages are broken into lines in
  requesters.
- 0.37 (2026-11-15, Nextcloud Handler): converting an empty text between
  the Amiga character set and UTF-8 could give leftover memory instead of
  an empty text (no case is known where the handler showed it).
- 0.32 (2026-11-15, Nextcloud Handler): reading stops with an error when
  the file is changed on the server during the read, instead of giving a
  mix of both versions. The handler's code is freed when the volume is
  dismounted (about 3 MB were lost with every mount). Problems that need
  the user, such as certificate errors, are shown in a requester once.
  Names with ":" from the server can be used (shown as %u003A). Files show
  the e bit, so programs on the volume can be started. Line breaks in
  requesters are shown correctly. Files over 2 GiB can be written with
  TEMPDIR on an FFS partition.
- 0.25 (2026-11-15, Nextcloud Handler): first test version.

webdav-handler is public domain. It uses libcurl, expat, zlib, clib4
and AmiSSL, see Third-party.txt for their licences.
